From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:21:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: configure VUI timing for HEVC

The firmware timing-info property is shared by H.264 and HEVC, but the
encoder only sets it for H.264, so HEVC streams carry no VUI timing and
don't describe the configured frame rate. Enable it for HEVC too. Keep
the H.264-specific entropy and filtering properties codec-specific.

[adeeb: drop a blank line before a closing brace]
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index 79acf7c1ec..bd47bec9a6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -687,11 +687,9 @@ static int venc_set_properties(struct venus_inst *inst)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (inst->fmt_cap->pixfmt == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264) {
+	if (inst->fmt_cap->pixfmt == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264 ||
+	    inst->fmt_cap->pixfmt == V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC) {
 		struct hfi_h264_vui_timing_info info;
-		struct hfi_h264_entropy_control entropy;
-		struct hfi_h264_db_control deblock;
-		struct hfi_h264_8x8_transform h264_transform;
 
 		ptype = HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_VUI_TIMING_INFO;
 		info.enable = 1;
@@ -701,6 +699,12 @@ static int venc_set_properties(struct venus_inst *inst)
 		ret = hfi_session_set_property(inst, ptype, &info);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
+	}
+
+	if (inst->fmt_cap->pixfmt == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264) {
+		struct hfi_h264_entropy_control entropy;
+		struct hfi_h264_db_control deblock;
+		struct hfi_h264_8x8_transform h264_transform;
 
 		ptype = HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_ENTROPY_CONTROL;
 		entropy.entropy_mode = venc_v4l2_to_hfi(
